    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d224">

                <pb facs="0319" n="215" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg215"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 493.11/457.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the American Minister.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-12-20">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 20, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Authorizes him to present each American claim upon its approval by the Department
                    and to urge the Diplomatic Corps to give priority to claims for actual losses
                    resulting directly from the revolution. His efforts to this end should not
                    commit this Government to the prejudice of such freedom of action as might be
                    necessary in case other Governments should support claims for actual but
                    indirect losses.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moore</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
